{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And he shall offer, etc.</b> The reason that HaShem fixed the measurements for the libations and for the oil of the meal-offering as a quarter-הin of oil per issaron, which is three log, and likewise a quarter-הin of wine for the libation; and for two issarons HaShem commands a third of a הin of oil and a third of a הin of wine, which is four log; and for three issarons, half a הin of oil and half a הin of wine, which is six log — so that it works out, according to the calculation, to two log per issaron, both for the meal-offering of two issarons and for the meal-offering of three issarons. Why then for the meal-offering of one issaron did HaShem require three log? This is along the lines of what is written in the Mishnah in Menahot (107a), and the Rambam wrote in chapter 17 of Hilkhot Ma'aseh HaKorbanot, and this is his language: \"A person may volunteer or vow wine on its own, but one does not volunteer one log of wine or two log, for among the libations there is neither one log nor two,\" end quote. And this is the reason of the verse, that it did not assign two log for one issaron, even though for two issarons a third of a הin sufficed, which is four log — to inform you that no offering of wine of two log is ever brought." "<b>And if</b> you say: this is well justified with regard to wine, but as for oil — we also find that it comes on its own as a freewill offering, for Rabbi Tarfon said (Zevaḥim 91a): \"A person may volunteer oil,\" and our Sages disagreed in Menahot (ibid.): some said not less than three log, and some said one may volunteer even one log, for the reason of דּוּן מִינָהּ וְאוֹקֵי בְּאַתְרָהּ — if so, according to the one who says not less than three log, the reason HaShem required three log for one issaron is well understood. But according to the one who says even one log — why did He not follow the calculation? One may say that HaShem equalized the measurements of oil and the measurements of wine in their offerings, a just principle for two and three issarons."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:09:50.883271358Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}